# Pet Horoscope Generator - Project Structure

This is a .NET Aspire-based Blazor Server application with the following architecture:

## Project Structure
- **PetHoroscopeGenerator.Web** - Main Blazor web application (UI layer)
- **PetHoroscopeGenerator.ApiService** - Backend API service
- **PetHoroscopeGenerator.ServiceDefaults** - Shared service configuration
- **PetHoroscopeGenerator.AppHost** - Aspire orchestration host
- **PetHoroscopeGenerator.Tests** - Unit and integration tests

## Key Files
- [Program.cs](mdc:PetHoroscopeGenerator.Web/Program.cs) - Web app entry point with service configuration
- [PredictionsApiClient.cs](mdc:PetHoroscopeGenerator.Web/PredictionsApiClient.cs) - AI prediction service client
- [MainLayout.razor](mdc:PetHoroscopeGenerator.Web/Components/Layout/MainLayout.razor) - Main application layout
- [NavMenu.razor](mdc:PetHoroscopeGenerator.Web/Components/Layout/NavMenu.razor) - Navigation menu

## Technology Stack
- **.NET 8** with Blazor Server
- **Azure OpenAI** for AI predictions
- **Azure Key Vault** for secrets management
- **.NET Aspire** for microservices orchestration
- **Bootstrap** for UI styling

## Page Structure
All pages follow the pattern: `@page "/route"` with `@rendermode InteractiveServer`